WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:09.966
Hello, my name is David Haas,

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:12.866
and in my previous presentation,

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:16.766
I explained to you how cryo-cooling was invented

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.832
and has contributed substantially

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:23.299
to the field of structural biology.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.999
And now, I'd like to give you an example

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.732
of an actual benefit that was derived from that,

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:31.166
which is the HIV epidemic

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.966
and some of the drugs

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:38.566
that were developed through structural biology.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.799
Once again, we need to thank Max Perutz,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.832
who began the field of structural biology

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.899
and had the great vision

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.566
that three-dimensional structures

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.166
not only permit the identification

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:55.732
of how the molecules act in living organisms

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:59.199
but in fact how the structures can be determined,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.899
as well as how drugs can now be designed

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.932
using the process called structure-based drug design.

00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:08.566
So, now I'd like to tell you a story

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:12.132
of how I have experienced

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:15.566
"science for the benefit of humanity."

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.066
While I was at the Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory,

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:21.199
I was told

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.132
that my cryo-cooling experiments and publications

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.232
probably advanced structural biology

00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:28.799
by 10 or 20 years.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.499
And at the time, you know,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.899
10 to 20 years of scientific discovery

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.532
is really usually not a big deal,

00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:37.166
and it didn't have any significance to me...

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:42.332
until while I was preparing for a presentation this last April,

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:45.766
at the Protein Data Bank in Rutgers,

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:49.699
they asked me to talk about exactly what I'm telling you:

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.832
the invention of cryo-crystallography.

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:53.499
And while I was doing that,

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.766
I discovered the AIDS epidemic

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.699
and the Lazarus effect.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.999
And for those of you who don't know

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.799
what the Lazarus effect is,

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.199
in medicine, the Lazarus effect

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.266
is when many people are dying

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.799
and then some event occurs

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.699
where these vast numbers of people stop dying.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.932
And that's exactly what happened

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.932
with the AIDS epidemic in 1996.

00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:22.999
This diagram here is from the United States

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.932
statistics from the CDC.

00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:27.666
But let me just tell you first about the worldwide AIDS epidemic,

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:31.199
which began in 1980.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.132
There have been 76 million people who have been

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.766
infected with HIV virus since 1980,

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.032
of whom 39 million have died.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.066
And today, worldwide,

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:47.499
there were 37 million people still infected.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.432
There is no cure for AIDS,

00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:51.566
as you know,

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:54.432
but there is a therapeutic treatment,

00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:56.299
and that's what I'm gonna explain.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.199
So, now if I can talk about the United States,

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.432
this is the death curve and the infection curve.

00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:04.599
The red one's the infection occur

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.499
for AIDS in the United States.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.499
So far, since 1980,

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.932
700,000 Americans have died from AIDS.

00:03:12.933 --> 00:03:15.499
And as you see,

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.166
the curve begins in 1980

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.132
and continually increases,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.766
with hundreds of thousands of individuals

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.332
becoming infected with AI...

00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:26.532
with HIV virus each year.

00:03:26.533 --> 00:03:28.332
Since the average lifetime,

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:31.466
if you had caught HIV in...

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.866
during the '80s,

00:03:33.867 --> 00:03:35.932
was typically 2-4 years,

00:03:35.933 --> 00:03:39.366
your statistics would move from the red curve to the blue curve,

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.466
which is the death rate,

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.399
in about 2 years.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.366
And you see that the death rate is continuous

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.466
from 1980 to 1996.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.532
It's a straight line, basically,

00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:51.799
which means that none of the drugs

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.832
-- and there were many drugs that were tried --

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:59.899
produced any effect on the death rate.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.332
In 1984,

00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:06.099
the HIV virus was identified as being

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.032
the causal agent of HIV.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.232
And then, in 1986,

00:04:10.233 --> 00:04:12.232
proteins were isolated,

00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:13.832
one of which is this protein,

00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:15.766
which is HIV protease,

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:19.932
one of the enzymes that makes the HIV virus.

00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:23.866
The crystal structure was actually determined,

00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:26.466
the three-dimensional structure, in 1989.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.732
And we can thank Merck Laboratory in New Jersey

00:04:29.733 --> 00:04:31.732
for not only solving the structure,

00:04:31.733 --> 00:04:34.666
but they published the data to the whole world

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.932
in the Protein Data Bank in 1989.

00:04:38.933 --> 00:04:41.366
This gave the opportunity

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.766
for hundreds of other laboratories

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:47.266
to work on the HIV protease.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:50.232
It turned out that inhibitors

00:04:50.233 --> 00:04:51.732
were actually made,

00:04:51.733 --> 00:04:54.432
and they were made using structural biology,

00:04:54.433 --> 00:04:56.366
using cryo-cooling.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:05:02.599
And in 1996, the therapy was introduced.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.132
It was this cocktail of three drugs,

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:09.266
of which the HIV protease inhibitor was the most important.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:12.166
And instead of dying, you would...

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:15.566
you would live a normal life,

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.799
with in fact...

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.499
it was called a manageable disease.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.932
And because of that,

00:05:21.933 --> 00:05:25.699
the individuals did not transfer to the death curve,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.332
and you see this precipitous fall

00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:30.666
in the death curve in 1996.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:34.132
The death rate fell from 96%

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.432
down to below 20%.

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:38.199
So, you can just imagine,

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.066
between 1980 and 1996,

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:44.132
if you had become infected with HIV

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.866
and you went to your physician,

00:05:45.867 --> 00:05:50.532
and he would tell you had a 4% chance of surviving.

00:05:50.533 --> 00:05:53.299
But in 1996,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:56.099
you would go in to... go to your doctor,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.199
and he would say, yes,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.832
today there's a therapy.

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:02.299
You will not be cured of HIV,

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.299
but it will in fact become a manageable disease.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.766
And this dramatic fall in the death rate in 1996

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.832
is called the Lazarus effect.

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:15.266
Tens if not hundreds of thousands of Americans

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:18.599
lived who would not live.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.699
And basically, the HIV protease inhibitor drugs

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.666
which were developed

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:26.999
were developed years and years faster

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.299
than they would have been

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.299
if there had not been structural biology,

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.566
and as it turns out, cryo-cooling,

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.966
which participated in that.

00:06:35.967 --> 00:06:37.832
So, it makes me feel very good

00:06:37.833 --> 00:06:40.999
that, literally, my research, done 50 years ago,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.499
not ending up in dusty pages in a journal

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.966
but actually saving thousands of lives.

00:06:46.967 --> 00:06:51.966
That really is science for the benefit of humanity.

00:06:51.967 --> 00:06:54.566
Experiments that you do,

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.099
and publications that you make,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.532
as a young scientist,

00:06:57.533 --> 00:06:59.699
will in fact... could contribute very much to the future.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:02.799
So, I hope you've become a little bit inspired

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.032
with the work that I have done,

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:06.966
and the fact that it inspired me,

00:07:06.967 --> 00:07:09.866
and maybe it will inspire you to continue.

00:07:09.867 --> 00:07:27.600
Thank you.

